Permissive licenses such as MIT and Apache-2.0 are **intentionally not used**:
they would allow a company to take this work, build a proprietary product on top
of it, and resell it **without any agreement with — or contribution back to —**
the author. The AGPL keeps the public version free and open while reserving the
commercial path for organizations that need proprietary terms, which they obtain
by purchasing a license.

